        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(admin-http-rpc): reject oversized declared request bodies",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Admin HTTP RPC callers could declare an oversized JSON request body with `Content-Length` above the 1 MiB limit and have the shared request reader tear down the socket before the route could deliver the structured 413 response.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Admin HTTP RPC handler now rejects well-formed oversized declared `Content-Length` values at the plugin route boundary before entering the shared body reader. The existing shared reader still handles missing, invalid, chunked, timeout, closed-connection, and malformed-JSON cases, so this stays local to the Admin HTTP RPC route and does not change the RPC allowlist, Gateway authentication, or method dispatch behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators and host tooling using `POST /api/v1/admin/rpc` get a clear HTTP 413 JSON response for oversized declared request bodies, and invalid oversized requests do not reach Gateway RPC dispatch.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: Admin HTTP RPC now delivers a structured 413 response to a real Node HTTP client for `Content-Length: 1048577`, and `dispatchGatewayMethod` is not called.\n- Current head: ec28f77e86fd6c1395f33337090b87cf9028e33b.\n- Focused regression: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/admin-http-rpc/src/handler.test.ts` passed with 1 file and 13 tests.\n- Sibling guard regression: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/http-body.test.ts` passed with 1 file and 13 tests.\n- Targeted lint: `node_modules\\.bin\\oxlint.CMD extensions\\admin-http-rpc\\src\\handler.ts extensions\\admin-http-rpc\\src\\handler.test.ts` passed.\n- Targeted format: `node_modules\\.bin\\oxfmt.CMD --check --threads=1 extensions\\admin-http-rpc\\src\\handler.ts extensions\\admin-http-rpc\\src\\handler.test.ts` passed.\n- Committed diff hygiene: `git diff --check HEAD~3..HEAD` passed.\n- Review proof: `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main --engine claude` passed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Observed result: the real HTTP regression starts a Node `createServer`, sends a Node HTTP client request declaring `Content-Length: 1048577`, receives HTTP 413 with `{ \"ok\": false, \"error\": { \"type\": \"invalid_request\", \"message\": \"Payload too large\" } }`, and verifies the Gateway dispatcher was not called.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the Admin HTTP RPC route boundary, shared SDK body guard behavior, focused tests, and ClawSweeper feedback before updating this PR.",
